  "methodology": "Rebuild the reviewed AVGO ordinary cash dividends on the source Close share basis, then retain the final Benjaminpo Adj Close / Close anchor. For other companies whose Adj Close differs by more than 1% at some date, add only reviewed regular cash dividends that the vendor's Adj Close omits, multiplying earlier Adj Close by (prior Close - amount) / prior Close. This is an adjusted historical price convention, not a tax-aware portfolio total-return simulation. Dividends the vendor applied wrongly (another company's, duplicated, or on the wrong scale) and a non-cash distribution it omitted are changed one by one in dividend_changes; each entry names the amount the vendor's series must show. A share exchange the vendor never recorded (share_exchanges) divides earlier Adj Close by the exchange ratio of the reviewed action in data/eps-split-rules.json, as analysis sites restate it; Close keeps the traded price.",
